                            "last_played": 1792623837
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Kingdoms and Castles is a really fun game that I'm really fond towards. I love the idea and execution (I mean it's a medieval city builder with diplomacy aspects and combat). I would say it's worth it's base price honestly because it is so polished it feels like a demo almost (I have never experienced bugs in vanilla).\n\nMy only wishes are bigger maps and multiplayer. They actually just recently increased max map sizes which is epic, though I still year for more. Multiplayer is something I've literally dreamt of (was a good dream) and would actually make this top 10 city builders for me, but I understand that MP can be nearly impossible to add for games that weren't developed with it in mind.\n\nIt can be cozy or insanely challenging depending on your gamemode and with mods (there's not many but there's a few gems), it is a really fun city builder.",
